Fix2 assertions
- Test 2: 200 entries after blocking node-2; rejoin observed via FakeNetwork. Every node-2 request batch is <= real RaftReplicationService.batchMax, maxActive<=1, matchIndex equals Leader lastLogIndex, log and commit converge, RPC count bounded.
- Test 8: creates an entry conflict at a follower's committed index and sends it through AppendEntries wire DTO. Conflicting write throws fail-closed, log/commit/original entry stay unchanged, Leader matchIndex stays unchanged, and later AppendEntries is refused.
- Test 9: 20 fixed seeds use Random(seed) drop/delay; timeout, invalid matchIndex, PEER_ERROR and transport failure synthetic replies do not advance matchIndex; network heals and all peers catch up to Leader lastLogIndex.
- Test 11: follower is persisted at a higher term, then a lower-term old-Leader request with a new entry and large leaderCommit is rejected success=false; log, commit, apply and vote stay unchanged, and the higher-term response steps the old Leader down without adding a successful match.
- Test 13: node-2 and node-3 are stopped while 30 entries are issued, then all rejoin. Each Node must have the Leader commitIndex/lastLogIndex/log, lastApplied==commitIndex, repo checkpoint=commitIndex and identical in-memory seat snapshot.

Scenario 12 - actual observation
- seed=53
- before disk loss: matchIndex[node-2]=24, commitIndex=24
- after follower storage reset: follower lastLogIndex=0
- final: matchIndex[node-2]=24, Leader commitIndex=24, nextIndex[node-2]=25, RPC count=28 over 200 rounds
- follower remains non-convergent/stuck.
- Leader commit/match did not decrease; majority prefix remained; no crash/unbounded loop.

